# T5: TIMED arm B of the ABAB timed pairs of the W2 window: A = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate (the control: the eight 262k seats, the nine best levers, the quad blocks, 19,968 blocks, the in-trace sampler), B = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w2 (wave 1 plus the multi-user SDPA launch and the conv-gates spread). Audits off in both arms. Arms run A B C A B C A B (T1-T8: three A-B pairs, each B right after its A, and two C runs, T3 and T6, each right after a B) in this one image, each after its own all-four reset. This job is wave 2.
# The tests: warmup, one coding stream, concurrent8_steady (the quad blocks' mix: the smoke rule needs it), eight 32k code users, eight about 120,000-token users (eight live at once) and the skewed eight (concurrent8_skew: two real-code prompts of about 253,920 tokens, users 0 and 4, one in each four-seat block, and six of about 4,096, as the server counts them, 800 out, started together: a multi-user SDPA launch on a fixed block geometry is paid at its longest user, so this is the shape where it can LOSE to per-user launches (the plan's row 7s: up to 9 ms a round at heavy skew) and the equal-length arms cannot show it).
# READ: the [PACKED-PHASE] round times of the eight-user tests, PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians (check the load average around the run: no build, no CI push and no other job beside it), the per-seat rate at 32k and at about 128k, the skewed eight's round time per round (the SDPA multi launch against the control at heavy skew: a loss there is the finding, not a failure), the texts equal between the arms, and on B: the lever lines
# (sdpa multi engaged and called, conv gates spread engaged with no fell-back line), the [PACKED-PRESTAGE] paths and [PACKED-HOSTGAP-WINDOW]. Then offline: python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 --position-keyed --strict-concurrent-prefixes (exit 0 identical).
# PROJECTION (the fusion plan's ladder): wave 2 reads a 32k round of about 159 ms and about 192 ms at 128k, 27.6 and 23.0 tok/s per seat, against 222 / 279 ms today and 182 / 236 ms for wave 1. THE LADDER'S WAVE 2 INCLUDES V5, WHICH THIS ARM LEAVES OUT (its byte gate has never run): read a few ms above 159 at 32k, and say so.
# THE WAVE'S OWN INCREMENT is read against the C runs, T3 and T6 (the W1 arm, same image, same tests, interleaved with the pairs), not against the control: the pair says what wave 1 plus wave 2 is worth, the C runs against the pair say what wave 2 adds to wave 1 (multi-user SDPA: +2 to 4% at short context, +6 to 17% at 128k as its own arm; F1: about -2 to -3 ms a round). B carries the same HOSTGAP_LOG as the C runs and the control does not.
# Duration (estimate): 130 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w2 eight-seat 262k wave-2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/w2 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_SUPERSEDED_BY=tp4-w2ln-jobs
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w2
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k,concurrent8_skew
